cff-version: 1.2.0
title: BlindCode Navigator
message: >-
  If you use this software or refer to it in academic work,
  please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Keleman
    given-names: Olha
    affiliation: Technische Universität Darmstadt
version: 0.2.0
date-released: '2026-11-01'
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/kelemano/blindcode-navigator'
abstract: >-
  A Visual Studio Code extension that makes the structure of Java
  source code audible for blind novice programmers. It separates
  movement along a nesting level from movement across levels,
  announces the surrounding scope in speech, and maps nesting
  depth to pitch. Developed and evaluated as part of a bachelor's
  thesis on structure-oriented audio navigation.
keywords:
  - accessibility
  - screen-reader
  - sonification
  - program-comprehension
  - computing-education
  - vscode-extension
  - tree-sitter
  - java
